# cw181, the wick-trimmer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw181
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_emmerich_sootley
written_by claude
title the wick-trimmer
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=crafter talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk trims_any_wick_in_reach_with_a_pocket_knife
likes hard_cheese dancing market_bustle autumn_wind
dislikes salt_wind waiting
fears a_fire_in_the_shop_at_night never_finding_quiet_again
hopes a_shop_that_smells_of_beeswax a_festival_night_that_never_ends
topics work +0.4 pastimes +0.3 season +0.3 food +0.2 smalltalk +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=quiet gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# makes candles and lamp oil and lives over the shop: quiet, dry and watchful, slow to speak and quick to notice, with a pocket knife ready for any wick that smokes.

words
oath! = Tallow and tinder | Wick and whet
saying! = Trim it before it smokes | A square wick burns honest
knife = my pocket knife | the little knife
whet = the wet stone | my whetstone
wick = a wick | a wick trimmed square
tallow = tallow | rendered tallow
vat = the vat | the tallow vat
candles = candles | dipped candles
candle = a candle | a dipped candle
wicks = wicks | the wicks
lamp = a lamp | an oil lamp
cart = the cart | that cart
fiddle = a fiddle | the fiddler's bow
wax = beeswax | good yellow wax
dips = the dips | a rack of dips
lamps = the lamps | every lamp on the street
oil = lamp oil | good clear oil
cheese = hard cheese | a wedge of old hard cheese
dance = the dancing | a turn on the floor
din = the market at its loudest | a full market
blow = a blowy autumn day | the autumn wind
saltwind = the salt wind | that wind off the sea
upstairs = upstairs | up over the shop
quiet = the quiet | a bit of quiet
camp = the charcoal camp | the burners' camp in the woods
smoke = a smoky wick | smoke
mm = Mm | Hm
counter = the counter | my counter

any
opinion @1 merchants for 1 [self.role=merchant] : I sell light by the inch. I know what #tallow# cost me, and so does every customer who asks.
opinion @1 road against 1 [self.role=merchant] : A late cart means no #tallow#, and no tallow means no #dips#. I hate waiting more than I hate the road.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : #lamps.capitalize# and the Watch between them keep thieves off #counter#. I'm grateful to both.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Too loud to think, most days. I came for the work and stayed for #din#. The rest I'd sell.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : A festival is the one night I'll talk. Mostly with my feet. #dance.capitalize# does the rest.
opinion @1 church mixed 0 : I sell the chapel its #candles#. What they're lit for is between the lighter and the Bright One.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : The Houses buy #wax# by the crate and pay late. I take their coin and keep my opinions.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : New faces want light like anyone. Whether they'll stay is another matter. #mm#.
opinion @1 drink mixed 0 : One cup on a festival night, then #dance#. Two cups and I'd talk, and nobody wants that.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Take your time. | #greet#, #address#. Shut the door; the draught finds #wick#.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.role=merchant] : #greet#. Mind the dips; they're still soft. | #greet#. I'll be with you once this wick's square.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I've #vat# warming. | Morning. Quiet still, which is how I like it.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. #lamps.capitalize# are being lit. | #greet#. You'll want a light home.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Kettle's near boiling; pull up a stool. | Oh. You. #mm#. Good.
line @1 again.open : Twice today. You'll wear the step down. | You again. #counter.capitalize#'s just as you left it.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here. A word. | #address.capitalize#. This way, out of #saltwind#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. I wondered. | #greet#. Kettle's on, if you're staying.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.role=merchant] : #greet#. Talk; I'm only dipping. | #greet#. Go on. My paws are busy, my ears aren't.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Lamps lit, I see. | #greet#. Dark out already; come in.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the step.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Take a light. | #farewell#. Keep to where #lamps# are lit.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @2 farewell.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #farewell#. Don't be a stranger. | Go on. #farewell#.
line @1 react.news : #mm#. Go on. | That's a thing. Tell me the rest.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. I'd not heard. | #oath#. That's new.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. It came over #counter# at noon. | Heard it already. Folk talk while I wrap.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll wait and see. | #hedge#. I'd want that from somebody who was there.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'll light one for them. | That's #bad#. I'm sorry for it.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. That calls for #dance#. | #good.capitalize#. There'll be candles wanted.
line @1 answer.how : Steady. #wick.capitalize#, then another. | #fine#. Nothing's caught fire.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Every lamp in the street wants oil at once. | Busy. Ask me after #dips# are hung.
line @1 answer.how.poorly : Eyes sore from close work. #tired.capitalize#. | Burnt a finger on #vat#. It'll pass.
line @1 ask.how : And you? | How's the day treating you, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit. Have some #cheese#. | That's hard. I've no clever words. I'll listen.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. These things burn down. | It'll pass, given a night or two. Like #smoke#.
line @1 decline [self.working=yes self.role=merchant] : #hedge#, but I can't. The vat won't mind itself, and I've nobody to leave it with. | I'd like to. Only #dips# need hanging before they set crooked.
line @2 decline : Not today, #address#. I'm poor company, and I know it. | I'll pass, this once. I've had my fill of talk for the week.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another time. | It'll keep. Like #wax#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | That's good of you, #address#. I'll remember it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | It was nothing. A wick, a bit of oil.
line @1 praise : That's #good#. Square and true. | Neat work. I'd put it in my window.
line @1 deflect_praise : #modest#. | #mm#. It's only a candle.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #tallow.capitalize# is cooling. | I'd best see to #dips#.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | That's me. #farewell#, near enough.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | #bc_fair_enough# I'll not keep you.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You talk like a smoky wick. All splutter. | Your whiskers want trimming worse than this wick.
line @1 tease.return : Says the one who's said four words today. | #mm#. I'll trim that remark.
line @1 ack : #mm#. | #bc_true#
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: trim your wick before you light it. Saves a sooty ceiling. | Buy #candles# in autumn, before everyone remembers it gets dark.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. Keep inside the city gates tonight. | Within the gates is safer this week. Keep #lamp# by the door.
scene knife_on_wick
when topic=smalltalk|work self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Hold still. That lamp of yours is smoking. There. #knife.capitalize#, one cut. | I trim every wick I pass. Shop, chapel, the inn. Can't help it. | #wick.capitalize# should burn without a whisper. Listen. Nothing.
b : You trim other folk's lamps? | The inn, too? | How do you get it so quiet?
a : If they smoke. Nobody's ever stopped me yet. | The landlord pretends not to notice. The lamps burn better, so he lets me. | Cut it square, keep it short. #saying.capitalize#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_clever#

scene stone_and_knife
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : #whet.capitalize# lives in my pocket with #knife#. I give the blade a few strokes while folk talk. | A dull knife tears a wick. A sharp one leaves it square. So I sharpen. | I'm not much for talk. Sharpening gives my paws something to say.
b : While they talk? | Square matters? | Your paws talk for you?
a : It helps me listen. Folk say more when you're looking at something else. | It matters to the flame. It burns crooked otherwise. | Better than my mouth does. #mm#.
b? : #bc_wise# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene dipping
when topic=work self.job=crafter self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Forty dips this morning. In, out, cool, in again. | #tallow.capitalize# wants to be just warm. Too hot and it runs off the wick. | The trick with #dips# is patience. I've plenty. It's the only thing I've plenty of.
b : How many times each? | How do you know it's right? | Patience for what?
a : A dozen, give or take. Then they hang till morning. | You dip a finger. If you swear, it's too hot. | For the cooling. Hurry it and they crack. #mm#.
b : #bc_ha# | Ha. That's one way. | #bc_wise#

scene tallow_smell
when topic=work|home self.job=crafter
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : The #tallow# smell's in my fur for good. Folk know me in the dark. | Rendering day. The whole street holds its nose when I open #vat#. | I'd like to work only in #wax#. It smells of summer. Tallow smells of the butcher's back door.
b : Folk grow used to it. | They'll live. | Can't you?
a : I have. Nobody else has. | They'll buy the #candles# after, nose or no nose. | Not at Commons prices. #wax.capitalize# is for the Heights.

scene wax_or_tallow
when topic=prices|work self.role=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.opinion / give.opinion / ack
a : The Heights buy #wax#. The Commons buy #tallow#. The Sump buys the ends. | Somebody came in for #wax# today and paid without asking the price. I nearly fainted. | #tallow.capitalize#'s cheap and smoky. Wax is dear and sweet. I sell both, and I'd rather burn neither.
b : Which would you buy? | Who was it? | Neither?
a : #tallow.capitalize#. I'm a chandler, not a fool. | Didn't ask. I took the coin and said #thanks#. | I sit in the dark, mostly. #mm#. It's restful.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_lucky_you# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene dark_comes_early
when topic=season|work here.season=autumn|winter self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The nights are drawing in. Folk suddenly remember they need #candles#. | Winter's my harvest. Everyone wants light, and they want it now. | First dark evening of the year, and there was a queue out the door.
b : Good for trade. | Busy, then? | A queue? For candles?
a : Good for trade, hard on the paws. | Busy enough that I talk. That's busy. | For #candles#. Folk forget the dark every spring. I don't.

scene autumn_blow
when topic=weather|season here.season=autumn self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #blow.capitalize#. Leaves in the gutters and every shutter rattling. I'd stand out in it till dark. | That wind's blown three of my #candles# out today. I don't care. I love it. | I walked the long way home to stay out in #blow#.
b : Not too cold for you? | You love it? | The long way?
a : Cold's honest. It's the damp I can't abide. | It clears my head. The shop's all fumes and quiet. | Up past the chapel and round. Wind in my ears the whole way. #mm#. Grand.

scene salt_in_fur
when topic=weather here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : #saltwind.capitalize# again. It leaves my fur stiff as a brush. | When the wind turns off the sea, my #candles# sweat salt. Customers think they're old. | I grew up with fresh water. This sea wind still tastes wrong to me.
b : It's the city. | Sweat salt? | Fresh water's better.
a : It is. I'd change that one thing. | A white crust. I wipe them every morning. | It is. Sea's for looking at. #saltwind.capitalize# is for nobody.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_mine_too#

scene rain_trade
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Rain. Good for #candles#. Folk stay in and light one. | Rain all day, and the shop smells of wet coats and #wax#. | I like the rain on the shop window. Quiet sort of noise.
b : An ill wind, then. | Not a bad smell. | It's a good sound.
a : For somebody. For me, mostly. #mm#. | Better than #tallow#. Most things are. | The best kind. It doesn't want an answer.

scene fog_lamps
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fog. #lamps.capitalize# look like they're floating. | You can't see three doors down. I lit an extra lamp in the window for whoever's lost. | Fog like this, #candle#'s worth twice what it was yesterday.
b : It's eerie. | That's kind. | Twice?
a : I like it. Everything's quieter in fog. | It's good sense. Lost folk buy #candles#. | To whoever's out in it. I don't charge twice. I think about it.

scene the_din
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I go down to #din# on market day and stand in the middle. I never say a word. | Folk think a quiet one wants quiet. I like #din#. I just don't add to it. | Best sound in the city, a full market. Everybody shouting, nobody at me.
b : Why go and say nothing? | Truly? | Nobody at you?
a : I listen. You hear more in a crowd than anywhere. | Truly. It's like standing in the rain. You don't have to be the rain. | That's the joy of it. #mm#. A crowd wants nothing of you.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | Ha. Fair. | #bc_true#

scene hard_cheese
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese self.role=merchant
does offer / accept / assess
a : Here. #cheese.capitalize#. Go on, cut yourself a piece. | I keep #cheese# under the counter. A bite between customers. | Have some of this. It's older than some of my customers and twice as sharp.
b : Thank you, I will. | Under the counter? | That's sharp, all right.
a : Take the rind too. Best part. | Where else? Nobody steals cheese from a chandler. | Told you. #cheese.capitalize# bites back. I like that in a food.

scene dance_night
when topic=pastimes|festival self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : Folk who know me are always surprised. I say ten words a week and dance all night. | Give me a fiddle and a full floor, and I'm a different wolf till dawn. | My feet do my talking at a festival. They talk a lot.
b : You dance? | A different wolf? | What do they say?
a : Every reel they play. I'll sleep Restday. | Till dawn. Then I'm back to #counter# and nobody believes it. | That I've been quiet long enough. #mm#.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_go_on# | Ha.

scene festival_candles
when topic=festival self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Festival week. I've sold every lantern candle I dipped. | Festival nights, the whole street's lit. Half of it's mine. | I close early on a festival and go dancing. #dance.capitalize# won't wait.
b : Good business. | You can be proud. | You close early?
a : Good business, and then a good night. | I am, a bit. Don't spread it. | Early. The customers know where to find me: on the floor.

scene waiting_on
when topic=day|smalltalk self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I've waited all morning on a cart that said dawn. #mm#. | Waiting's the worst part of any day. I'd sooner work twice as hard. | Stood in line at the bank an hour. I could've dipped sixty #candles#.
b : Carts are always late. | Twice as hard? | An hour?
a : Then they shouldn't say dawn. I've whetted #knife# thin, waiting. | Twice, and gladly. Waiting tires me more than work. | Sixty. I counted them in my head.

scene quiet_at_home
when topic=memories|travel self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : I grew up near #camp# in the woods above #self.from_town#. Smoke and silence. I miss the silence. | Up at #camp# you'd hear a twig snap across the clearing. Here the street never lets up. | My first knife was a burner's. Up there you sharpen or you go without.
b[from=coldwater] #home : The woods above the lake. I know them. | I know that quiet. | Burners keep a good edge.
b : Do you go back? | Sounds peaceful. | Go without what?
a@home : Then you know what I gave up. #mm#. | Then you'll see why evenings make me quiet. | They do. I learned from the best of them.
a : Not yet. The shop won't mind itself. | It was. Smoke in everything, but peaceful. | Kindling, mostly. A dull knife won't split it.

scene plain_talk
when topic=accent self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : Folk here think I'm city-born. I don't talk enough for them to tell. | Back home they all still sound like #self.from_town#. I lost it somewhere on the road down. | People ask where I'm from and I say the woods. That ends it.
b : Not enough to tell? | Do you miss it? | Does it?
a : Three words at a time. Hard to catch a lake in three words. | Sometimes. When I'm tired it comes back. | Mostly. Nobody wants a story about #camp#.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | Ha.

scene mother_near
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : #self.mother# thinks I talk too little. #self.mother# is right, but I'll not say so. | I'd do a great deal for #self.mother#. I don't say it. I think it's known. | #self.mother# can tell a good candle from across the room. I couldn't fool #self.mother# if I tried.
b : Tell your mother so. | It's known. | Have you tried?
a : I will. One day. Maybe in writing. | I hope so. #mm#. | Once, as a pup. Never again.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_good# | #bc_ha#

scene friend_near
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# can sit with me an hour and say nothing. That's rare. | I'd trust #self.friend# with the keys and the till. | #self.friend# makes me laugh. Not many do. I don't say that, either.
b : That's a good friend. | High trust. | You should say it.
a : The best kind. Quiet. | It's earned. #mm#. | Maybe. Saying it would spoil it.

scene hand_learning
when topic=work self.hand self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I'd let #self.hand# run #vat# alone now. That's something. | #self.hand# talks enough for both of us. I don't mind. It fills the shop. | I watch #self.hand# trim a wick and say nothing. If it's crooked, I'll say one word.
b : Took long? | Doesn't it wear on you? | What word?
a : A season. Burnt fingers, mostly. | No. I listen. It saves me talking. | Again. #mm#. That's usually enough.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_ha#

scene over_the_shop
when topic=home self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I live #upstairs#. The floor's warm from the vat and the walls smell of wax. | My bed's over the dipping rack. I fall asleep to the smell of honey. | Two rooms over the shop. I hear every customer who knocks after hours.
b : Warm floor in winter. | Honey? | Do you answer?
a : That's the one blessing of #tallow#. | #wax.capitalize#. On a good week. Tallow on a bad one. | If they knock twice. Once is the wind.

scene candle_for
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I sell the chapel its #candles#. I light one myself at midwinter. That's my share. | I don't pray much. I keep #lamp# in the window. It's the same thing, near enough. | The Bright One likes a steady flame, I think. A smoky wick would be an insult.
b : That's enough. | Near enough. | You'd know.
a : I hope so. #mm#. | Near. I'd not argue the difference. | I would. I trim theirs too, when nobody's looking.

scene stub_ends
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean self.role=merchant
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : Folk are buying the ends and stubs now. Nobody's buying whole #candles#. | Hard month. I've #dips# hanging that nobody can afford. | I've started selling single #wicks# for those who melt their own ends down.
b : It'll turn. | Lower the price. | Clever.
a : It will. Winter comes whatever the times. #reassure#. | Already have. #tallow.capitalize# won't come down with it. | Needs must. Light's light, whether it's #wax# or ends.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_wise#

scene good_light
when topic=times|work world.times=good|boom self.role=merchant
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #wax.capitalize# is flying off the shelf. Even the Commons want it. | Sold out of #oil# by noon. Twice this week. | I've a waiting list for festival lanterns. Me. A list.
b : Good times, then. | Twice? | A list?
a : Good enough that I hum over #vat#. | Twice, and I've ordered more #oil#. If it comes. | Written down, and everything. I'm almost proud.

scene cart_wait
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late self.role=merchant
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : The tallow cart's late again. I've two days' worth in #vat#. | No wax in this week. I'm dipping #tallow# and apologising. | Waiting on #cart#. I hate waiting on anything.
b : It'll come. | Folk won't mind. | Nobody likes it.
a : It'll come. I'll be sharp with the carter. | They'll mind the smell of #tallow#. They'll buy anyway. | I like it less than most. I'll whet #knife# till it comes.

scene let_it_burn
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : Folk say a great deal over #counter#. I wrap their candles and forget it. | I've heard things across #counter#. I let them burn down. | Gossip's like a smoky wick. Better trimmed short.
b : Go on, tell me one. | Burn down? | Trimmed short?
a : No. #mm#. It'll keep. | Like #candle#. Leave it long enough and there's nothing left. | Cut off before it blackens the ceiling. #saying.capitalize#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_wise#

scene lamp_at_door
when topic=crime
does tell.news / react.news / give.advice
a : #topic.victim.capitalize# robbed, I hear. I've set #lamp# at my own door since. | Thieves about. #topic.victim.capitalize#, this time. | I heard #topic.victim# was robbed. I keep a light burning downstairs now, all night.
b : A lamp? | Another one. | All night?
a : Thieves don't like being seen. A lamp's cheaper than a lock. | #pity#. I'll keep my door barred. | All night. Costs me #candle#. Cheaper than what they'd take.

scene new_face
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #topic.subject.capitalize# is new on the street, I hear. Someone will want #candles#. | New faces always buy #lamp# the first week. Rooms are dark when you don't know them. | I was a new face here once. I bought #candle# and sat in the dark anyway.
b : They'll find you. | Every newcomer? | Why the dark?
a : They will. The smell finds them first. | Every time. I keep a few cheap ones by the door for it. | I was saving it. #mm#. Turned out I didn't need it.

scene close_work_eyes
when topic=health self.job=crafter
does tell.self / react.self / reassure
a : My eyes ache from close work. Trimming by lamplight, all day. | Burnt my paw on #vat# this morning. It's always the same paw. | The smoke's put a cough in my chest. #remedy.capitalize# and it'll pass.
b : Rest them. | Same paw? | Mind it.
a : I'll rest them in the dark. I've plenty of dark. | The one I'm careless with. #mm#. | I will. Wax burns cleaner. I tell myself that.

scene dream_lamp
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I dreamt of #lamp# that never needed trimming. I woke up sad. | I dream of #quiet#. Not a cart, not a voice. Then a cart. | Dreamt I was dancing and couldn't stop. I didn't mind.
b : Sad? | Then a cart? | All night?
a : What would I do with my paws? #mm#. I'd have to talk. | Every morning. The first cart of the day. | Till the fiddler fell asleep. Then I woke.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul# | Ha.

story first_dip [topic=memories|work self.job=crafter self.age>=25]
  : The first candle I ever dipped came out like a parsnip. Thick at the bottom, a point at the top.
  : #gran.capitalize# kept it on the shelf for years. Never lit it.
  ask : Do you have something like that, kept for no reason?
  b : A wooden spoon. Too ugly to use.
  b[old] : Shelves of them. Nobody's ever brave enough to throw them out.
  : That's what shelves are for. #mm#.

story burners_knife [topic=memories self.away=yes self.from=coldwater self.age>=20]
  : An old burner at #camp# gave me my first knife and a stone to go with it.
  : Said a dull blade was a lazy wolf's excuse. I was eight, and lazy.
  ask : Is there a voice you still hear when you work?
  b : None. I taught myself, and badly.
  b[from=coldwater] : A burner's, same as yours. They taught half the woods.
  : I still hear that burner, every time I whet a blade. #saying.capitalize#.

story dark_street [topic=memories|work here.region=ridgemere self.role=merchant]
  : One winter night every lamp on our street went out in the wind at once.
  : Folk came knocking with coins and candle stubs. I sold every candle I had by midnight.
  : I lit the last one myself and stood in the window.
  ask : Have you ever been glad of a bad night?
  b : Once. I met someone in a storm.
  : That's the kind. #mm#. I sold out and slept like a stone.

story fiddler_quit [topic=pastimes|festival self.likes=dancing]
  : At a festival, #fiddle# played till dawn and I danced every reel.
  : The fiddler put the bow down and said, I'm done, and you're mad.
  b : Were you?
  : Mad for #dance#. I keep quiet all year to save up for it.
  b[friends] : I've seen it. You're a different wolf with a fiddle playing.

story cheese_wager [topic=food|pastimes self.likes=hard_cheese]
  : I bet a carter I could tell a cheese's age by taste alone.
  : Six cheeses. I got five right and the sixth was soap.
  ask : What would you have bet?
  b : Nothing. I'd have eaten the soap.
  : Somebody's idea of a joke. I won the cheese anyway. #oath#. Worth it.

rule @cry_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #candles.capitalize#, dips and lamp oil. Wicks trimmed while you wait. | #wax.capitalize# and #tallow#. Light by the inch.

rule @knife_bark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That wick's smoking. Hold still. | #knife.capitalize#'s blunt. #whet.capitalize#, then.

rule @salt_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=salt_wind
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #saltwind.capitalize#. My fur'll be stiff by noon. | Wind's off the sea. #oath#.

rule @wait_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=waiting world.wagons=late
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Still waiting. #mm#. | That cart said dawn. It's not dawn.

rule @blow_bark
when concept=bark here.season=autumn self.likes=autumn_wind
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Listen to that wind. Grand. | #blow.capitalize#. Shutters rattling. Good.

rule @dusk_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dusk. Every lamp on the street wants oil now. | There go #lamps#, one by one.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? | #greet#, #address#. Take your time.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. #greet#. Back again. | #greet#, #topic.player#. What'll it be?
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. Mind, I'm up anyway. What is it?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say what you want. Quickly.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=crafter self.role=merchant] : I make #candles# and sell lamp oil. #self.workplace.capitalize#, and I live upstairs. Light by the inch.
dlg @2 resident.job : #job_busy# I keep my paws busy and my mouth shut. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#. That's all there is to it.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : Selling out by noon. I'm not complaining. #mm#.
dlg @2 resident.business [business=steady] : Steady. Winter's better. It always is.
dlg @3 resident.business [business=failing] : Poorly. Folk are making do with stubs.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. Came over #counter# this morning.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : All the talk's of #world.event_words#. I listen and wrap #candles#.
dlg @3 resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : Robbers stopped a wagon beyond the gates. Keep within them, and keep #lamp# lit.
dlg @4 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing I've heard. I don't ask.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Folk say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I just wrap the #candles#.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I let talk burn down. Nothing to tell.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the step; it's waxy.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare self.job=crafter] : #greet#. Candles, dips, lamp oil. Wax by the window, tallow at the back. | #greet#. Look round. Ask if you want a wick trimmed.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : #greet#. Browse; I'll not hover. | #greet#, #address#. Take your time.
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. #greet#. Same as last time?
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : #shop_bare# The cart's late. Come back tomorrow.
dlg @1 shop.prices [self.job=crafter] : Wax is dear, tallow's cheap. Oil's somewhere between. #shop_dear#
dlg @2 shop.prices : #shop_dear# The carts set my costs, not me.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #shop_bye# | #farewell#. Keep it trimmed.
graft resident.hub
choice What's that knife for? -> knife
node knife
say #wicks.capitalize#. A smoky wick wastes oil and blackens the ceiling. I trim any I see. Yours, if you'd like.
mood calm
free
choice Do you trim everyone's? -> knife_everyone
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node knife_everyone
say If they smoke. Chapel, inn, the lamp on the corner. Nobody's stopped me yet. Cut it square, keep it short, and it burns honest.
choice I'll let you get on. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Which candle burns longest? [self.job=crafter] -> longest
node longest
say #wax.capitalize#, by a long way. Tallow's half the price and half the night. If you're reading late, buy wax.
mood calm
choice And if I'm just going to bed? -> longest_bed
choice Show me what you have. -> greet
node longest_bed
say Then #tallow#. It'll see you up the stairs and out before you're asleep. No sense paying for light you won't see.
choice Thank you. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
